<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBQA-F003-F004-AN15HTTPFUZZ>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBQA-F003-F004-AN15HTTPFUZZ" ;
  triage:title "boundary-probe and differential-probe vary a label never read by production code (RBQA-F002 defect class recurrence)" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr's AN15HTTPFUZZ-QA-1 verdict found that 2 of 4 HTTP fuzz probes (boundary-probe, differential-probe) vary labels attached to request elements that production code never reads -- so all 100 cases in each of those 2 probes hit identical code branches, producing false appearance of coverage diversity. Same defect class as RBQA-F002, now recurring in the HTTP test suite. Boundary-probe varies retired provenance header; differential-probe varies Accept header. Shape-probe and template-probe confirmed genuinely diverse." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-an" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "test-quality" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-15T04:16:42Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AN.15 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-15T04:16:42Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:resolutionNotes "Update 2026-08-15 by quality-mgr, AN15HTTPFUZZ-QA-2: fix commit 9681de8a5 independently re-verified via ruthless-boundary-qa, PARTIAL FIX only. The differential-probe occurrence (lib.rs:2006) is genuinely fixed: its 5 rewritten cases against /v1/atm/messages/search each trace to a distinct real branch inside decode_search_query (message_handler.rs:488-527) with unique expected_message assertions per branch -- closing that occurrence. The boundary-probe occurrence (message_handler.rs:1047) is NOT fixed -- still open, reproduces the same defect class this record was filed for. Shape 0 (retired-header presence) is a genuine distinct branch, but the remaining 4 of 5 labeled shapes collapse into only 2 real axum branches: shape-slots 1 ('missing-content-type') and 2 ('non-json-content-type') both hit axum's identical json_content_type()-false rejection (axum 0.8.9 json.rs:130,138-155) regardless of header-absent vs header-wrong; shape-slots 3 ('json-syntax') and 4 ('json-data', body `{\"to\":true` -- missing closing brace) both hit Category::Eof -> JsonSyntaxError (axum json.rs:176-179), not Category::Data as claimed, because the body is truncated rather than well-formed-but-wrong-typed. Corroborating: the test's own expected_message for shape-slots 1-4 is the identical hardcoded literal across all four. Recommendation from reviewer: use a complete, well-formed-but-wrong-typed body (e.g. `{\"to\":true}`) to genuinely reach Category::Data, and either collapse the claimed shape count to 3 real branches or replace the redundant slot with a body that fails at a different layer. NOT closing this record -- keeping status open pending a further fix round on the boundary-probe occurrence only. Update 2026-08-15 by quality-mgr, AN15HTTPFUZZ-QA-3: fix commit cc0ee308e (evidence refresh 68c9c3192) independently re-verified via ruthless-boundary-qa -- boundary-probe now genuinely FIXED. Case-shape table shrank from 5 nominal slots to 4 real slots (message_handler.rs:985-990: retired-header, non-json-content-type, json-syntax, json-data), each with a distinct expected_message. json-data body is now complete/well-formed-but-wrong-typed (`{\"to\":true}`, closing brace present) which reaches AgentAddress's map-only Deserialize impl (address.rs:96-101) and produces a serde_json::error::Category::Data via JsonRejection::JsonDataError (framework_rejection, message_handler.rs:571-583), genuinely distinct from json-syntax's truncated-body Category::Eof/JsonSyntaxError. Axum confirmed still 0.8.9 (Cargo.lock:361-363), consistent with the prior round's branch analysis. Differential-probe, shape-probe, template-probe confirmed unchanged (68c9c3192 is evidence-log/report refresh only, no code diff). CI green 9/9 on cc0ee308e/68c9c3192. Both occurrences now fixed -- closing this record." ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RBQA-F003-F004-AN15HTTPFUZZ/boundary-probe-1047> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RBQA-F003-F004-AN15HTTPFUZZ/differential-probe-2006> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "3" .

